      "page_title": "Inspecting Live Tasks",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Is a Live Task?"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==asyncio.all_tasks()== returns the set of **pending** tasks on the running loop",
            "Call it inside the loop. With no running loop it raises `RuntimeError`",
            "==asyncio.current_task()== returns the task running this coroutine",
            "Use it for logging and to leave yourself out of `all_tasks()`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "t = asyncio.create_task(",
            "    poll(), name=\"poller\")",
            "t.set_name(\"poller-eu\")",
            "print(t)  # name='poller-eu'"
          ],
          "note": "named tasks beat 'Task-17' in dumps"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Reading a Task's State"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "Gives you"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`get_stack(limit=None)`",
              "suspended frames"
            ],
            [
              "`print_stack(limit, file)`",
              "the stuck **await**"
            ],
            [
              "`get_coro()`",
              "wrapped coroutine"
            ],
            [
              "`done()` / `cancelled()`",
              "finished? cancelled?"
            ],
            [
              "`exception()`",
              "error it raised"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "fr = t.get_stack()[-1]",
            "print(fr.f_code.co_name,",
            "      fr.f_lineno)  # where",
            "print(t.get_coro())"
          ],
          "note": "last frame = the stuck await"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Why names matter",
          "text": "`create_task(coro, name=...)` and `set_name()` put the name in reprs, logs and every task dump."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Hang Dump & Leak Check"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "me = asyncio.current_task()",
            "for t in asyncio.all_tasks():",
            "    if t is not me:",
            "        t.print_stack(limit=5)"
          ],
          "note": "run it when the test hangs"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@pytest_asyncio.fixture",
            "async def no_leaks():",
            "    yield",
            "    left = asyncio.all_tasks()",
            "    left.discard(asyncio.current_task())",
            "    assert not left, left"
          ],
          "note": "leftovers mean fire-and-forget bugs"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Exclude ==current_task()== from every dump",
            "`print_stack(file=sys.stderr)` to keep it in CI logs",
            "Leftover task? **Await** it, cancel it, or keep a ref"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Python 3.14: Outside View"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Shows"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`python -m asyncio ps PID`",
              "tasks of a live process"
            ],
            [
              "`python -m asyncio pstree PID`",
              "the task **tree**"
            ],
            [
              "`asyncio.print_call_graph()`",
              "chain of awaiting tasks"
            ],
            [
              "`capture_call_graph()`",
              "same, as data"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "`print_stack()` shows **one** task's frames. The ==call graph== follows task A awaiting B awaiting C across tasks, and the CLI works from __outside__ the process.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        }
      ],
