      "page_title": "Hang Recipe & Task States",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Hung in production?",
          "text": "On 3.14, `python -m asyncio pstree PID` needs no code change and no restart."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Expecting `all_tasks()` to list **finished** tasks. It only reports pending ones",
            "Calling `all_tasks()` from another thread. It only sees the running loop",
            "Calling it outside a loop gives `RuntimeError`",
            "Dumping every task, yourself included. Filter out `current_task()`",
            "Leaving tasks unnamed, so the dump is full of `Task-17`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Hang Recipe",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Wrap the test body in `asyncio.timeout(5)`",
            "On ==TimeoutError==, dump every other task",
            "Read the **last** frame of each stack",
            "Fix the unset Event or missing `await` there"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "try:",
            "  async with asyncio.timeout(5):",
            "    await run()",
            "except TimeoutError:",
            "  for t in asyncio.all_tasks():",
            "    t.print_stack(limit=3)",
            "  raise"
          ],
          "note": "turns a silent hang into a dump"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Task State Cheatsheet",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
