    {
      "page_title": "Deterministic Tests for Timeouts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What to assert",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Assert the ==outcome==: `TimeoutError` was raised",
            "Assert the side effect: cleanup / `finally` **ran**",
            "Never assert real elapsed seconds (`< 1.0`)",
            "Wall-clock checks get __flaky__ when CI is under load"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Timeout primitives"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Scope",
            "Fires"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`asyncio.timeout(d)`",
              "a block (3.11+)",
              "after d s"
            ],
            [
              "`wait_for(aw, t)`",
              "one awaitable",
              "after t s"
            ],
            [
              "`timeout(0)`",
              "a block",
              "next **await**"
            ],
            [
              "past deadline",
              "a block",
              "next **await**"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Since 3.11 `asyncio.TimeoutError` **is** builtin ==TimeoutError==",
            "`timeout(0)` = instant timeout, zero sleeping",
            "`await asyncio.sleep(0)` yields exactly ==one step==",
            "Use it so pending callbacks run before an assert"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Force it: await forever"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "from asyncio import timeout",
            "ev = asyncio.Event()  # never set",
            "with pytest.raises(TimeoutError):",
            "  async with timeout(0.01):",
            "    await ev.wait()"
          ],
          "note": "never finishes, so it always times out"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def job():",
            "  try: await ev.wait()",
            "  finally: cleaned.append(1)",
            "with pytest.raises(TimeoutError):",
            "  async with timeout(0):  # instant",
            "    await job()"
          ],
          "note": "then assert cleaned == [1]"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "After a timeout the inner task is ==cancelled==",
            "Check `task.cancelled()` and the cleanup side effect",
            "Proves cancellation handling, not just the raise"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Flaky vs deterministic"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flaky",
            "Deterministic"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`sleep(0.5)`, hope order",
              "test-owned ==Event/Future=="
            ],
            [
              "real backoff sleeps",
              "patch `asyncio.sleep`"
            ],
            [
              "wait a real 60 s",
              "==virtual time=="
            ],
            [
              "hope callbacks ran",
              "`await sleep(0)`"
            ],
            [
              "assert elapsed",
              "assert `TimeoutError`"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "sl = AsyncMock()",
            "with patch(\"svc.sleep\", sl):",
            "  await retry(flaky)  # instant",
            "got = [c.args[0] for c in",
            "       sl.await_args_list]",
            "assert got == [1, 2, 4]"
          ],
          "note": "patch where retry looks it up"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Dependency finishes when **you** call `fut.set_result(x)`",
            "Inject a `clock` into code that reads time",
            "==looptime== fast-forwards `loop.time()`",
            "A 60 s timeout then runs in milliseconds"
          ],
          "style": "star"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`task.cancelled()` is **True**",
            "The `finally` side effect happened",
            "No tasks left in ==all_tasks()=="
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "Outcomes, not seconds"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cancellation & Controlling Order",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "try: await work()",
            "except asyncio.CancelledError:",
            "  pass  # ✗ swallowed!"
          ],
          "note": "always re-raise CancelledError"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Swallowing ==CancelledError== inside timed code",
            "`timeout` can't convert it, so the timeout **silently** fails",
            "Asserting elapsed time instead of the outcome",
            "Never checking that cleanup ran after cancel"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "try: await work()",
            "except asyncio.CancelledError:",
            "  await cleanup()",
            "  raise  # ✓ timeout still works"
          ],
          "note": "clean up, then re-raise"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Checking Cancellation",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "t = asyncio.create_task(job())",
            "await asyncio.sleep(0)  # start",
            "t.cancel()",
            "with pytest.raises(CancelledError):",
            "  await t",
            "assert t.cancelled()"
          ],
          "note": "sleep(0) lets the task start first"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. wait_for vs timeout",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "wait_for",
            "timeout"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "form",
              "call",
              "`async with`"
            ],
            [
              "wraps",
              "one awaitable",
              "whole block"
            ],
            [
              "move deadline",
              "no",
              "`cm.reschedule()`"
            ],
            [
              "since",
              "any",
              "3.11+"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. You Control the Order",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "fut = loop.create_future()",
            "t = asyncio.create_task(svc(fut))",
            "await asyncio.sleep(0)",
            "assert not t.done()  # waiting",
            "fut.set_result(1)",
            "assert await t == 1"
          ],
          "note": "the test decides when it finishes"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "sleep(0) is one step",
          "text": "Need more than one step? Await the Event or Future, don't stack `sleep(0)` calls."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Assert ==outcomes==, never seconds",
            "Test-owned Events and Futures set the order",
            "Patch `sleep`, or use ==virtual time==",
            "Check cleanup ran after every timeout"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "Outcomes, not seconds"
    },
